    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d703">

                <pb facs="0732" n="720" sameAs="frus:frus1945v08/pg720"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">867N.01/8–1345: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Consul General at Jerusalem</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Pinkerton</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Jerusalem</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1945-08-13T15:00:00+03:00">August 13, 1945—3
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 7:17 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>146. My telegram 141, August 9, 11 a.m. Palestine Government has authorized
                    joining August and September quotas permitting entry <pb facs="0733" n="721"
                        xml:id="pg721"/> 3,000 in either month. Action taken because shipping
                    difficulties make arrival Mauritius refugees during August doubtful. This makes
                    provision for group referred to in Department’s telegram 147 August 6<anchor
                        n="13" xml:id="d703-f1"/> and prevents charge of deliberate stretching of
                    White Paper quota if either month is filled.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Pinkerton</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
